    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling performance today, anchored by the standout matchup for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). Facing Griffin Canning, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable SP_xERA, a +14% platoon edge, and a +5% boost from wind-out conditions at the park, making him our primary engine for stolen base production. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (71.16) remains a must-start despite the neutral park, as his elite 0.444 xwOBA provides an immense floor for R and RBI production. **Caleb Durbin** (65.50) and **Carson Benge** (64.91) also emerge as core contributors; **Caleb Durbin** exploits a soft matchup against Mikolas, while **Carson Benge** leverages his leadoff spot to capitalize on the favorable projection against Yesavage.\n\nOur bench decisions were constrained by a flurry of \"Lineup Pending\" designations, forcing us to lean heavily on historical assumptions. The closest call for the starting nine was **Dillon Dingler** (57.36), who narrowly held his spot over other middle-tier options due to a favorable dynamic platoon split against Weathers and a specific speed advantage\u2014the opposing pitcher's slow delivery creates a high-leverage environment for stolen bases, which we are prioritizing as a scarcity play. While **Gary Sanchez** (54.62) and **Casey Schmitt** (55.46) are currently slated in, their scores remain marginal; should their official lineups slide down the order, we may consider defensive substitutions to protect game caps.\n\nRisks for this slate are primarily situational. We are monitoring the status of **Christian Yelich** and **Luke Raley**, whose scores could fluctuate significantly once their respective batting positions are confirmed. Additionally, while **Trea Turner** (56.83) and **Kyle Schwarber** (53.96) are active, they face a stiffer test against the higher-tier skill of Ashcraft. With **Junior Caminero**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Rece Hinds**, and **Colt Keith** all unavailable due to off-days, minors assignments, or benchings, our active roster depth is thinner than usual, placing a premium on the performance of our top-heavy core to maintain our 5x5 standing.",
